From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:11:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: vdpu381: reset the cores together once they
 are idle

The k4d board run showed every timeout right after a core reset: a core
failed on a broken stream (errors that fail without the CCU too), was
reset at once, and the frame the other core was decoding at that moment
never finished (CCU core status still busy for both cores), costing the
stream on the other core a frame -- two fluster vectors that pass on
their own (HCBP1_HHI_A, HCHP3_HHI_A) failed next to failing ones.

In CCU mode the cores wait for each other, so do what the BSP's soft-CCU
worker does (rkvdec2_soft_ccu_worker(): reset only "if
(!rkvdec2_core_working(queue))"): when a core fails or times out, start
no new job, take the later frames of the same stream that the other
cores decode off their watchdogs (they predict from the failed one and
can't finish), let the other jobs finish, then reset all the cores and
run the m2m job that was held back. Without a CCU a failed core is still
reset at once.

The failed job, and those later frames, keep their cores and are only
completed once the cores are reset: until then, a core may still be
decoding into their buffers, or hold a bus transaction in its IOMMU, and
their runtime PM references keep the IOMMUs from being suspended (which
disables paging) under them.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-h264.c     |   5 +-
 .../rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-hevc.c     |   5 +-
 .../media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c   | 202 ++++++++++++++++--
 .../media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.h   |   9 +-
 4 files changed, 205 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-h264.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-h264.c
index 69967c34fffa..85206ed7322e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-h264.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-h264.c
@@ -481,6 +481,7 @@ static int rkvdec_h264_run(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	struct rkvdec_h264_ctx *h264_ctx = ctx->priv;
 	struct rkvdec_h264_priv_tbl *tbl = rkvdec_h264_priv_tbl(ctx)->cpu;
 	struct rkvdec_h264_run run;
+	int ret;
 
 	rkvdec_h264_run_preamble(ctx, &run);
 
@@ -501,7 +502,9 @@ static int rkvdec_h264_run(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	rkvdec_run_postamble(ctx, &run.base);
 
 	/* Before the watchdog: this may wait for the earlier frames. */
-	rkvdec_job_wait_poc_alias(ctx);
+	ret = rkvdec_job_wait_poc_alias(ctx);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	rkvdec_schedule_watchdog(core, h264_ctx->regs.common.reg032_timeout_threshold);
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-hevc.c
index beb876a909a3..d67e9e05a2dc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-hevc.c
@@ -634,6 +634,7 @@ static int rkvdec_hevc_run(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	struct rkvdec_hevc_ctx *hevc_ctx = ctx->priv;
 	struct rkvdec_hevc_job_tbl *job_tbl = rkvdec_hevc_job_tbl(ctx);
 	struct rkvdec_hevc_priv_tbl *tbl = job_tbl->priv_tbl.cpu;
+	int ret;
 
 	rkvdec_hevc_run_preamble(ctx, &run);
 
@@ -657,7 +658,9 @@ static int rkvdec_hevc_run(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	rkvdec_run_postamble(ctx, &run.base);
 
 	/* Before the watchdog: this may wait for the earlier frames. */
-	rkvdec_job_wait_poc_alias(ctx);
